  "PhotoPath": "",
  "Caption": "CQRS: split reads from writes.\n\nCommands change state through the domain model in one transaction. Queries are read-only, project straight into DTOs, and can use a denormalized read model. They are just two handlers \u2014 a command side and a query side.\n\nYou don\u0027t need event sourcing or a second database to do CQRS. Reach for it when reads and writes scale or shape differently; skip it for simple CRUD.\n\nAre you using CQRS, and how far did you take it?\n\n#DotNet #CSharp #CQRS #SoftwareArchitecture #CleanArchitecture",
